    <section class="empire-glance" id="at-a-glance" aria-labelledby="glance-title">
      <div class="empire-glance-main"><h2 class="empire-glance-title" id="glance-title">At a glance</h2><ul><li>A county on the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/scheldt">Scheldt</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sambre">Sambre</a>, ruled from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mons">Mons</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/valenciennes">Valenciennes</a>, within the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/holy-roman-empire">Holy Roman Empire</a> but facing <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a>.</li><li>Its counts became <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/latin">Latin</a> emperors of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/constantinople">Constantinople</a> and married into the French and English royal houses.</li><li>Absorbed by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/burgundy">Burgundy</a> in 1433 and partly lost to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a> in 1659–1678, it was annexed by revolutionary France in 1795.</li></ul></div>
      <aside class="empire-dyk"><p class="empire-dyk-title">Did you know?</p><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/philippa-of-hainaut">Philippa of Hainaut</a>, queen of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/edward-iii-of-england">Edward III</a>, took the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/valenciennes">Valenciennes</a> chronicler <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jean-froissart">Jean Froissart</a> into her service, giving him access to the English court for his chronicles.</p></aside>
    </section>

